                <pb facs="0576" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/814: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-23T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Your telegram no. 8, January 19, 10 p.m. Referring to the confidential note
                    mentioned in the above telegram. In confidential interview the Chilean
                    Ambassador has stated that he intends to suggest that it be changed by the
                    elimination of references to conversations, etc., and that he will suggest
                    substitute phraseology. His action is entirely voluntary. If the Government of
                    Chile should <pb facs="0577" n="457" xml:id="pg457"/> care to withdraw the note
                    referred to above, substituting for it another that covers the same points in
                    another manner, the Department authorizes you to accept the substitution, but
                    unless the Minister of Foreign Affairs indicates a desire to change his note do
                    not mention this matter to him; should he do so, confine yourself to saying that
                    you are authorized, as a result of conversations of the Chilean Ambassador with
                    me, to accept the substitute note.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
